{
  "name": "Triage campaign replies with your own AI agent",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Triage campaign replies with your own AI agent\n\n### How it works\nLet your own AI model sort the inbox, with clear limits. Every new reply starts the workflow; the trigger adds the conversation ID. The workflow reads the whole thread and hands it to the agent. The agent loads your reply statuses, sets the one that fits, blocks the address when someone asks to stop, takes a wrong person out of the campaign, and returns a two-line summary that is posted to Slack. The agent has no tool to send email, so nothing goes out to the prospect.\n\nArgorant actions here are free. Your model provider bills its own usage.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Activate the trigger with your Argorant credential. Argorant webhooks come with the Pro plan, and your n8n needs a public HTTPS address.\n4. Pick a chat model in **Chat model** (any chat model node works) and add its credential.\n5. Read the rules in **Reply triage agent** and adapt them.\n6. Add a Slack credential and channel to **Post the summary**.\n\n### Customization\nAdd your own pipeline stages in Argorant; the agent reads them with Get reply statuses.",
        "height": 643,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "3c6e2e47-95c6-4a24-8d47-e40cfd1bcf3d",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Your AI model\nAny chat model node works. It decides; the tools act in Argorant.",
        "height": 120,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "e7b938cb-43ab-4610-940a-16d0625e40f5",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Allowed actions\nLabel, block and remove only. There is no tool that sends email.",
        "height": 120,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "517b008a-800c-4bf7-b994-4d90bedf45a6",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        520,
        420
      ]
    },
